on\\\": \\\"e1e3806b4b20c7f3df4116109007824843baf86a71970d45c5011687ab71f4b0\\\",\\n    \\\"test/goldens/g2-edge-exclusion.json\\\": \\\"851d12966180e109525394d059f82c2fbc566ada959240781f236759939686c9\\\",\\n    \\\"test/goldens/g3-oversized-loner.json\\\": \\\"0268d5c71cb4c85abf2841d36edac2b17703cb4c1767083e6831cd0a308c0754\\\",\\n    \\\"test/goldens/g4-turnless-straggler.json\\\": \\\"b1b3f482c2598a07e292150db7f6222574e5e25d800c6d6b57938fbbe75f5daf\\\",\\n    \\\"test/view-sweep.test.ts\\\": \\\"6b3fe356ec8b2ee55525acfc56cae73f13204ac4381f9019468342f9ee2477f2\\\",\\n    \\\"test/view-boundary.test.ts\\\": \\\"4afaf519dbcdcc85a111066e620fd2837d4ca83872c8356c875d806a70f639fc\\\",\\n    \\\"test/goldens/boundary-g1-trajectory.json\\\": \\\"a655e4cceb8be02b1a34f6974776acd07545b3f1061e0cf16e6635373d787ed4\\\",\\n    \\\"test/view-render-targets.test.ts\\\": \\\"a3195b6b56fbc1dc27b4bdd62b6cb717c3b2e0308fab92d711501125709e60c0\\\",\\n    \\\"test/cli-process-view.test.ts\\\": \\\"f1f3c4e5b36f80c4510065fc24db5faa6c1de2890447a866d5869a63dd96f51c\\\",\\n    \\\"test/messages-read.test.ts\\\": \\\"0b6c53ae2a1c1c4cc8de303d39d978912e9d83907895379b4b3f80c39ce163c3\\\",\\n    \\\"test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts\\\": \\\"19742b4c1693586313196fbf64eced4ab64e3d981df32c7c825c758f0f180cd3\\\",\\n    \\\"test/inspect-overview.test.ts\\\": \\\"e7aebfc5020e3addd1f17123977cf48646be5db03b6a0d1ebcc5f9ff65bb4969\\\",\\n    \\\"test/inspect-health.test.ts\\\": \\\"4e395d873c3469674d1829310d84afa508ad4eabf2a3e10fec1240f9c120fb4a\\\",\\n    \\\"test/inspect-view.test.ts\\\": \\\"b631376bfff9edeed0d11c2e324440254d0573fe4d02785fca1c9d081370a921\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_37\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'pnpm vitest run test/inspect-view.test.ts'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_37\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'pnpm vitest run test/inspect-view.test.ts'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\\n RUN  v4.1.8 /Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc\\n\\n(node:31745) ExperimentalWarning: SQLite is an experimental feature and might change at any time\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n\\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\\n      Tests  7 passed (7)\\n   Start at  11:01:32\\n   Duration  852ms (transform 133ms, setup 0ms, import 283ms, tests 487ms, environment 0ms)\\n\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_38\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md | sed -n '120,215p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_39\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/03-view-contents-report.md | sed -n '1,140p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_38\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md | sed -n '120,215p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"   120\\t  \\\"view\\\": { \\\"viewId\\\": \\\"v391\\\", \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"…\\\", \\\"compactPoint\\\": 391, \\\"coveredFrom\\\": 12 },\\n   121\\t  \\\"visibility\\\": { \\\"boundaryPosition\\\": 398, \\\"zoneTokens\\\": 18204 }\\n   122\\t}\\n   123\\t```\\n   124\\t\\n   125\\t### Flow 2: View Contents Report\\n   126\\t\\n   127\\t```\\n   128\\tinspect.view ──► threadView.describe ──► stored arrangement/gaps/config/band tokens/source state\\n   129\\t      │\\n   130\\t      └────────► threadView.pull ──► served messages\\n   131\\t                      │\\n   132\\t                      ├─ band entries → cross-check count only (arrangement is describe's)\\n   133\\t                      └─ tail entries → estimator → tailTokens (as served: short forms short)\\n   134\\tloadCost = { bandTokens: Σ stored, tailTokens: measured, total: sum }\\n   135\\t```\\n   136\\t\\n   137\\tNever-compacted: `describe` → null ⇒ `meta: null`, bands empty, whole pull output is tail, parity contract unchanged (AC-2.4). The report never recomputes selection, rendering, or boundary state — stored snapshot + live pull are the only sources (AC-2.1's \\\"not recomputed\\\" is structural).\\n   138\\t\\n   139\\t### Flow 3: Message Listing and Show\\n   140\\t\\n   141\\t`listMessages(ref, opts)`: existing read + WHERE bounds on `source_event_order`, LIMIT, deleted filter (default excluded; `includeDeleted` includes flagged). `show(ref, messageId)`: by-id read, full blocks verbatim from the record, `deleted` flag honest, forms from `report({messageId})`. Not-found → `message_not_found` (existing code). Deleted + show → `ok` with flagged record (AC-3.3: audit, never not-found).\\n   142\\t\\n   143\\t### Flow 4: Health\\n   144\\t\\n   145\\t`health(ref)`: `messages.report` + `turns.report` (full, not-ready included) + `listQueuedWork` both owners. Compose: counts by owner/kind/state from report entries' states; `failures[]` from `failed`/`blocked` entries (reason, attempts, lastError off `FormReportEntry`); `repairPreview[]` = failed-and-not-blocked subjects (reported, never requeued — AC-4.3); `queue` = queued/claimed counts from the live-item joins, consistent by construction with the same entries' states (AC-4.5). Rebuild visibility (AC-4.4) is two health calls bracketing a drain — no new mechanism, the cascade's pending states simply show.\\n   146\\t\\n   147\\t### Flow 5: Lifecycle Exercise\\n   148\\t\\n   149\\tScripted in `test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts`: phases named `create | intake | drain | status | compact1 | pull1 | inspect1 | mutate | rebuild | health2 | compact2 | pull2 | materialize`. Each phase returns its results to the driving test; checkpoint assertions live in the test, not the script. Teardown leg (TC-5.3) re-creates the SDK between named phase groups using the same script with a `freshSdk` hook. Receipt-vs-health cross-check (AC-5.2): `compact2`'s receipt sweep section against the `health2` snapshot taken immediately before — field-level equality on the failed/requeued sets.\\n   150\\t\\n   151\\t## Interface Definitions\\n   152\\t\\n   153\\t`src/shared/inspect.ts` (load-bearing shapes; field comments carry AC refs in source):\\n   154\\t\\n   155\\t```typescript\\n   156\\texport interface InspectOverview {\\n   157\\t  thread: { id: string; createdAt: string; metadata?: Record<string, string> };\\n   158\\t  events: { count: number; span: { first: number; last: number } | null };\\n   159\\t  messages: { visible: number; byKind: Record<string, number>; deleted: number; visibleTokens: number };\\n   160\\t  turns: { open: number; closed: number };\\n   161\\t  chunks: { count: number; unchunkedTurns: number };\\n   162\\t  derivation: { ready: number; pending: number; retrying: number; failed: number; blocked: number };\\n   163\\t  view: { viewId: string; createdAt: string; compactPoint: number; coveredFrom: number } | null;\\n   164\\t  visibility: { boundaryPosition: number; zoneTokens: number };\\n   165\\t}\\n   166\\t\\n   167\\texport interface ViewContentsReport {\\n   168\\t  meta: { viewId: string; createdAt: string; profile: string | null;\\n   169\\t          config: { lowerBound: number; percentages: Record<string, number> };\\n   170\\t          compactPoint: number; coveredFrom: number } | null;\\n   171\\t  bands: Array<{ band: Band; entries: Array<{ subjectKind: \\\"chunk\\\" | \\\"turn\\\"; subjectId: string;\\n   172\\t          formUsed: string; degraded: boolean }>; storedTokens: number }>;\\n   173\\t  gaps: Array<{ band: Band; subjectId: string; reason: string }>;\\n   174\\t  tail: { messageCount: number; tokens: number };          // as served (AC-2.2)\\n   175\\t  loadCost: { bandTokens: number; tailTokens: number; total: number }; // = pull (AC-2.3)\\n   176\\t  sourceState: { maxEventOrder: number; formCounts: Record<string, number> }; // provenance verbatim (AC-2.5)\\n   177\\t}\\n   178\\t\\n   179\\texport interface HealthReport {\\n   180\\t  owners: Array<{ owner: \\\"messages\\\" | \\\"turns\\\"; kind: string;\\n   181\\t          counts: { ready: number; pending: number; retrying: number; failed: number; blocked: number } }>;\\n   182\\t  failures: Array<{ owner: string; subjectKind: string; subjectId: string; form: string;\\n   183\\t          reason: string; attempts: number; lastError?: string }>;\\n   184\\t  repairPreview: Array<{ owner: string; subjectKind: string; subjectId: string; form: string }>;\\n   185\\t  queue: { queued: number; claimed: number };\\n   186\\t}\\n   187\\t```\\n   188\\t\\n   189\\tSurface signatures:\\n   190\\t\\n   191\\t```typescript\\n   192\\t// inspect\\n   193\\toverview(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<InspectOverview>>;\\n   194\\tview(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<ViewContentsReport>>;\\n   195\\thealth(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<HealthReport>>;\\n   196\\t// thread-view addition\\n   197\\tdescribe(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<StoredView | null>>;   // StoredView mirrors the row: id, createdAt, compactPoint, coveredFrom, profileName, config, arrangement, gaps, sourceState, bands (band → storedTokens)\\n   198\\t// messages additions\\n   199\\tlistMessages(ref: ThreadRef, opts?: { from?: number; to?: number; limit?: number; includeDeleted?: boolean }): Promise<OpResult<MessageRecord[]>>;\\n   200\\tshow(ref: ThreadRef, messageId: string): Promise<OpResult<MessageDetail>>;  // MessageRecord (full blocks, deleted flag) + forms: FormReportEntry[]\\n   201\\t```\\n   202\\t\\n   203\\tCLI grammar (JSON stdout, existing error classes, exit conventions inherited):\\n   204\\t\\n   205\\t```\\n   206\\tlhc inspect overview --thread <ref>\\n   207\\tlhc inspect view     --thread <ref>\\n   208\\tlhc inspect health   --thread <ref>\\n   209\\tlhc messages list    --thread <ref> [--from <n>] [--to <n>] [--limit <n>] [--include-deleted]\\n   210\\tlhc messages show    --thread <ref> --message-id <id>\\n   211\\t```\\n   212\\t\\n   213\\tError codes: no additions. `thread_not_found`, `message_not_found`, `caller_error` (bad bounds: `from > to`, `limit < 1`), `state_corruption`, `system_error` — all existing.\\n   214\\t\\n   215\\t## Testing Strategy\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_39\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/03-view-contents-report.md | sed -n '1,140p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# Story 3: View-Contents Report\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t### Summary\\n     4\\t<!-- Jira: Summary field -->\\n     5\\tExpose the stored active view through `threadView.describe` and report view contents with load-cost parity to `pull`.\\n     6\\t\\n     7\\t### Description\\n     8\\t<!-- Jira: Description field -->\\n     9\\t**User Profile:** The operator audits what the agent actually saw; agents inside a harness use the same read mid-task.\\n    10\\t\\n    11\\t**Objective:** Report stored view bands, gaps, provenance, tail cost, and total load cost without recomputing the view.\\n    12\\t\\n    13\\t**Scope In:** `threadView.describe`, `inspect.view`, `lhc inspect view`, stored snapshot reporting, tail cost as served, load-cost equality with `pull`.\\n    14\\t\\n    15\\t**Scope Out:** No view derivation, repair, mutation, provider invocation, or direct inspect-domain reads of `thread_view` tables.\\n    16\\t\\n    17\\t**Dependencies:** Epic 03 Stories 0-2 landed for view storage and `pull`; Story 2 inspect surface conventions available.\\n    18\\t\\n    19\\t### Acceptance Criteria\\n    20\\t<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\\n    21\\t- **AC-2.1**: The report names the active view — viewId, createdAt, profile name and resolved config, compactPoint, coveredFrom — and lists every band entry in served order (brief → detailed → smooth): subject kind and id, form used, degraded flag; plus every gap with its reason; plus per-band stored token counts. All of it from the stored snapshot, not recomputed.\\n    22\\t\\n    23\\t- **AC-2.2**: The tail section reports message count and token cost *as currently served*: tool results at-or-behind the visibility boundary are costed at their short form, everything else full.\\n    24\\t\\n    25\\t- **AC-2.3**: `loadCost` totals what `pull` serves now — bands plus tail — and a test asserts equality against an actual pull's measured content. The report never disagrees with the surface it describes.\\n    26\\t\\n    27\\t- **AC-2.4**: A never-compacted thread reports view: null with a tail-only loadCost under the same equality contract (the whole record served as tail).\\n    28\\t\\n    29\\t- **AC-2.5**: The report carries the view's recorded source-state provenance (what the compact saw: max event order, form counts) and is a pure read under AC-1.4's contract.\\n    30\\t\\n    31\\t- **TC-2.1** (AC-2.1, AC-2.5): On a compacted fixture with one degraded entry and one gap → report matches the stored arrangement exactly: subjects, forms used, degraded flags, gap reasons, band token counts, config, provenance.\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t- **TC-2.2** (AC-2.2, AC-2.3): On a boundary-advanced fixture → tail cost counts short forms short; `loadCost.total` equals the token measure of an actual `pull`'s messages using the same estimator.\\n    34\\t\\n    35\\t- **TC-2.3** (AC-2.4): Never-compacted thread → view null, tail spans the record, cost-parity assertion holds.\\n    36\\t\\n    37\\t### Technical Design\\n    38\\t<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\\n    39\\t#### Architecture Context\\n    40\\t\\n    41\\tThis story adds the single thread-view surface Epic 04 needs: `threadView.describe`. It exposes the stored active view row from the owning domain so inspect never reads thread-view tables directly.\\n    42\\t\\n    43\\t`inspect.view` combines `describe` and `pull`. The stored arrangement, gaps, config, stored band tokens, and source-state provenance come from `describe`; tail cost comes from measured pull output, making load-cost parity structural.\\n    44\\t\\n    45\\t#### Build Strategy\\n    46\\t\\n    47\\tStrategy: tdd-lite\\n    48\\t\\n    49\\tReason:\\n    50\\t- The story has one governing contract, but `loadCost` can drift if implementers reimplement pull selection or boundary-aware shortening.\\n    51\\t\\n    52\\tRisk Reminders:\\n    53\\t- `describe` must return the stored snapshot, not recompute it.\\n    54\\t- Never-compacted threads return `meta: null`, empty bands, and tail-only cost.\\n    55\\t- `inspect.view` inherits served tail behavior from `pull`.\\n    56\\t\\n    57\\t#### Implementation Targets\\n    58\\t\\n    59\\t| Area | Files / Modules |\\n    60\\t|------|-----------------|\\n    61\\t| Thread-view surface | `src/domains/thread-view/index.ts` |\\n    62\\t| Inspect internals | `src/domains/inspect/internal/view-report.ts` |\\n    63\\t| Inspect surface | `src/domains/inspect/index.ts` |\\n    64\\t| Shared shapes | `src/shared/inspect.ts` |\\n    65\\t| CLI/SDK | `src/cli/inspect.ts`, `src/sdk.ts` |\\n    66\\t| Tests | `test/inspect-view.test.ts` |\\n    67\\t\\n    68\\t#### Design References\\n    69\\t\\n    70\\t- [tech-design.md §Spec Validation](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:12), lines 12-22\\n    71\\t- [tech-design.md §Module Boundaries](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:54), lines 54-98\\n    72\\t- [tech-design.md §Storage](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:100), lines 100-102\\n    73\\t- [tech-design.md §Flow 2: View Contents Report](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:125), lines 125-137\\n    74\\t- [tech-design.md §Interface Definitions](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:151), lines 151-213\\n    75\\t- [test-plan.md §TC → Test Mapping](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:20), lines 20-40\\n    76\\t- [test-plan.md §Architecture-Risk Tests](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:42), lines 42-50\\n    77\\t- [test-plan.md §Chunk Red/Green Detail](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:56), lines 56-64\\n    78\\t\\n    79\\t#### Test Mapping\\n    80\\t\\n    81\\t| TC | Test File / Check | Test Description |\\n    82\\t|----|-------------------|------------------|\\n    83\\t| TC-2.1 | `test/inspect-view.test.ts :: arrangement fidelity` | Report entries, forms, degraded flags, gap reasons, config, and provenance equal `describe` output and stored row. |\\n    84\\t| TC-2.2 | `test/inspect-view.test.ts :: loadCost parity on boundary-advanced fixture` | Tail costs short forms short and total equals estimator over an independent pull. |\\n    85\\t| TC-2.3 | `test/inspect-view.test.ts :: never-compacted` | `meta: null`, empty bands, tail spans the record, and cost parity holds. |\\n    86\\t\\n    87\\t#### Architecture-Risk Tests\\n    88\\t\\n    89\\t| Risk | Test File / Check | Test Description | Why AC/TC Mapping Alone Would Miss It |\\n    90\\t|------|-------------------|------------------|---------------------------------------|\\n    91\\t| Load cost drifts from served reality | `test/inspect-view.test.ts` independent-pull leg | Measure report total against a second pull's served messages. | A report can look plausible while disagreeing with what agents actually receive. |\\n    92\\t| Inspect reads thread-view storage directly | `check-boundaries` plus source check | Inspect must consume `threadView.describe` and `threadView.pull`. | Direct table reads could pass fixture assertions while violating ownership. |\\n    93\\t| Describe mutates or recomputes | `test/inspect-view.test.ts` describe legs and read-only delta helper | Null/shape behavior and before/after state equality are asserted. | Stored snapshot fidelity requires source and side-effect checks, not just output fields. |\\n    94\\t\\n    95\\t#### Technical Notes\\n    96\\t\\n    97\\t- `threadView.describe` returns ok/null for absent views.\\n    98\\t- `inspect.view` should not recompute arrangement, form choice, gaps, or source-state provenance.\\n    99\\t- `loadCost.bandTokens` sums stored band counts; tail tokens are measured from pull's served tail.\\n   100\\t\\n   101\\t#### Anti-Shim Requirements\\n   102\\t\\n   103\\t- Compare report content to stored row data and to independent pull output.\\n   104\\t- Do not fake parity by sharing a helper that bypasses `pull`.\\n   105\\t- Do not create new storage or migration to support this read.\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\t#### Production Path Proof\\n   108\\t\\n   109\\t- Entrypoint: `threadView.describe`, `inspect.view`, `lhc inspect view`.\\n   110\\t- Registration/default path: `src/sdk.ts` exposes `threadView.describe` and inspect view; `src/cli/inspect.ts` routes `view` to SDK.\\n   111\\t- Evidence: default-suite inspect-view tests plus process checkpoint parity in the lifecycle story.\\n   112\\t\\n   113\\t#### Verification\\n   114\\t\\n   115\\t- Targeted: `pnpm verify`\\n   116\\t- Story gate: `pnpm verify`\\n   117\\t- Epic/process gate: `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all`\\n   118\\t\\n   119\\t#### Spec Deviations\\n   120\\t\\n   121\\tNone.\\n   122\\t\\n   123\\t### Definition of Done\\n   124\\t<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n   125\\t- `threadView.describe` exposes the stored active view row read-only and returns null when absent.\\n   126\\t- `inspect.view` reports stored bands, gaps, config, provenance, tail, and loadCost.\\n   127\\t- `loadCost.total` equals measured `pull` content for compacted and never-compacted threads.\\n   128\\t- `lhc inspect view` returns SDK-parity JSON.\\n   129\\t- TC-2.1 through TC-2.3 pass with one primary owner in this story.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_40\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md | sed -n '20,65p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_40\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md | sed -n '20,65p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"    20\\t## TC → Test Mapping\\n    21\\t\\n    22\\t| TC | Test (file :: name) | Assertion spine |\\n    23\\t|----|--------------------|-----------------|\\n    24\\t| TC-1.1 | inspect-overview :: full shape variants | fresh-empty, mid-first-turn, never-compacted-with-record, compacted, and mid-rebuild all return the full shape with absent pieces as zeros/nulls; compacted fixture exact counts per section vs fixture ground truth |\\n    25\\t| TC-1.2 | inspect-overview :: deleted accounting | delete one → visible−1, deleted=1, kind map excludes, tokens drop by its estimate, event count unchanged |\\n    26\\t| TC-1.3 | inspect-overview :: purity | two calls, no writes between → deep-equal; read-only delta assert green; zero provider calls |\\n    27\\t| TC-2.1 | inspect-view :: arrangement fidelity | entries/forms/degraded/gap reasons/config/provenance equal `describe` output equal stored row (degraded + gap fixture) |\\n    28\\t| TC-2.2 | inspect-view :: loadCost parity on boundary-advanced fixture | tail costs short forms short; `total` = estimator over an independent `pull`'s messages |\\n    29\\t| TC-2.3 | inspect-view :: never-compacted | `meta: null`, bands `[]`, tail spans record, parity holds |\\n    30\\t| TC-3.1 | messages-read :: order, fields, bounds | record order; kind/tokens/turnId present; `from`/`to`/`limit` exact windows; `from > to` → `caller_error` |\\n    31\\t| TC-3.2 | messages-read :: show full record + forms | drained tool-result: full content (not shortened), forms with states, outcome metadata present |\\n    32\\t| TC-3.3 | messages-read :: deleted handling | default list excludes; `includeDeleted` marks; show on deleted → ok + flag; show on missing id → `message_not_found` |\\n    33\\t| TC-3.4 | cli-process-inspect :: list/show parity | spawned `lhc messages list/show` JSON deep-equals in-process SDK results |\\n    34\\t| TC-4.1 | inspect-health :: counts + queue consistency | mixed-state fixture: exact counts per owner/kind/state; queue section equals live-item counts from the same reports |\\n    35\\t| TC-4.2 | inspect-health :: failure detail + preview | failed: reason/attempts/lastError exact; blocked excluded from preview; preview = failed∧¬blocked set exactly |\\n    36\\t| TC-4.3 | inspect-health :: rebuild bracket | edit → health: cascade set pending with queued work visible (exact subjects per cascade contract); `drainSettled` → same set ready; disjoint forms untouched |\\n    37\\t| TC-5.1 | lifecycle :: full sequence + checkpoints | every phase ok; post-compact pull = bands+tail; mutate → pending; drain → ready; compact2 reflects edit; receipt sweep section field-equals pre-compact health snapshot |\\n    38\\t| TC-5.2 | lifecycle :: replay determinism | fresh thread, same script → hash-equal pull outputs and materialized file |\\n    39\\t| TC-5.3 | lifecycle :: teardown continuity | `freshSdk` between phase groups → final pull/health/file identical to TC-5.1 run |\\n    40\\t| TC-5.4 | cli-process-inspect :: checkpoint parity | spawned CLI overview/view/list at three checkpoints deep-equal in-process results at same checkpoints |\\n    41\\t\\n    42\\t## Architecture-Risk Tests\\n    43\\t\\n    44\\t| Risk | Test | Why it bites |\\n    45\\t|------|------|--------------|\\n    46\\t| Inspect quietly writes (work rows, boundary nudge, view touch) | **read-only delta assert**: shared helper snapshots observable state (queued work via owners, boundary/zone via status, view identity via describe, event/message counts) before/after *every* new operation; deep-equal after. Runs inside each TC file via wrapper | A single forgotten side effect makes \\\"inspect describes, never changes\\\" fiction; absence-of-delta is checkable, absence-of-write-code is not |\\n    47\\t| Zero-provider on all new ops | suite-wide assert extended: overview/view/health/describe/show/list under a throwing provider config → all ok | The no-inference NFR stays structural through the last epic |\\n    48\\t| `loadCost` drifts from served reality | TC-2.2's independent-pull leg + lifecycle TC-5.1 checkpoint (report at compact1 vs pull1) | Parity by construction can still break at the estimator seam; two independent measurements pin it |\\n    49\\t| Health re-derives instead of composing | health tests assert composition through owner surfaces only: `check-boundaries` forbids cross-domain internal imports, an Epic 04 source check rejects raw SQL references to other domains' tables from `domains/inspect/**`, and the read-only delta assert separately catches writes | The must-not-own rule is the domain's entire contract |\\n    50\\t| Lifecycle order bugs only visible cross-epic | TC-5.1's named-phase checkpoints; receipt-vs-health field equality | First sequence ever to run all surfaces in PI-extension order; seam drift between three separately-built epics surfaces here or in production |\\n    51\\t\\n    52\\t## Suite Accounting\\n    53\\t\\n    54\\tDefault suite grows ~26 tests across 5 files. Process suite grows TC-3.4 + TC-5.4 (2 spawned scenarios, ~6 assertions); accounting row carried: process suite `ran | not-ran` recorded per verify-all invocation, never silently skipped.\\n    55\\t\\n    56\\t## Chunk Red/Green Detail\\n    57\\t\\n    58\\t**Chunk 1 — message reads (S1).** Red: `show` absent from surface (structured not-implemented per house stub rule); list opts ignored — bounds test fails on full-list return. Green: opts → WHERE/LIMIT; show + report join; `cli/messages-read.ts`; TC-3.1–3.3 + read-only legs. ~8 tests.\\n    59\\t\\n    60\\t**Chunk 2 — inspect domain (S2).** Red: `inspect.*` stubs return not-implemented; fixture lacks mutation-variant (TC-4.3 unwritable → fixture work first). Green: `shared/inspect.ts` shapes; overview composition; health composition; `cli/inspect.ts`; delta-assert helper lands here and wraps Chunk 1's ops retroactively. TC-1.1–1.3, TC-4.1–4.3. ~11 tests.\\n    61\\t\\n    62\\t**Chunk 3 — view report (S3).** Red: `describe` absent; `inspect.view` stub. Green: `describe` (row → `StoredView`), `view-report.ts` (describe + pull → report), TC-2.1–2.3 + describe null/shape legs. ~6 tests.\\n    63\\t\\n    64\\t**Chunk 4 — lifecycle (S4).** Red: `lifecycle.ts` helper absent; all four TC files reference it. Green: script with named phases + `freshSdk` hook; TC-5.1–5.3 default; TC-5.4 process. ~7 tests (4 scenarios, multi-checkpoint).\\n    65\\t\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"artifactsRead\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/03-view-contents-report.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/03-view-contents-report/003-implementor.json\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/snapshot.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/render.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/view-report.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/overview.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/shared/inspect.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/cli/inspect.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/cli/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/scripts/check-boundaries.mjs\",\"packages/lhc/test/inspect-view.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/read-only-delta.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/red-manifest.json\",\"packages/lhc/package.json\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Initial verification of Story 3: threadView.describe, inspect.view, CLI/SDK exposure, TC-2.1 through TC-2.3 tests, configured gates, and production-path audit for direct inspect storage reads or fake runtime paths. No files were edited.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-03-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Unruled public contract deviations remain in inspect.view report shape\",\"evidence\":\"Story technical notes say loadCost.bandTokens sums stored band counts (03-view-contents-report.md:95-100), and the epic Flow 2 design states loadCost = { bandTokens: Σ stored, tailTokens: measured, total: sum } (tech-design.md:127-135). The same interface definition makes sourceState non-null (tech-design.md:167-177). Implementation instead computes bandTokens from served pull band messages in view-report.ts:67 and makes sourceState nullable in shared/inspect.ts:70-74; tests assert the measured-band behavior and null never-compacted sourceState in inspect-view.test.ts:241-245 and inspect-view.test.ts:351-356. The implementor artifact records both as specDeviations, but I found no artifact showing an impl-lead/product ruling. AC-2.3 also requires loadCost.total to equal measured pull content, so the authoritative public contract cannot be established from current evidence.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/03-view-contents-report.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/03-view-contents-report/003-implementor.json\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/view-report.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/shared/inspect.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/inspect-view.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.3\",\"AC-2.4\",\"AC-2.5\",\"TD-Flow-2\",\"TD-Interface-ViewContentsReport\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-03-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Unruled public contract deviations remain in inspect.view report shape\",\"evidence\":\"Story technical notes say loadCost.bandTokens sums stored band counts (03-view-contents-report.md:95-100), and the epic Flow 2 design states loadCost = { bandTokens: Σ stored, tailTokens: measured, total: sum } (tech-design.md:127-135). The same interface definition makes sourceState non-null (tech-design.md:167-177). Implementation instead computes bandTokens from served pull band messages in view-report.ts:67 and makes sourceState nullable in shared/inspect.ts:70-74; tests assert the measured-band behavior and null never-compacted sourceState in inspect-view.test.ts:241-245 and inspect-view.test.ts:351-356. The implementor artifact records both as specDeviations, but I found no artifact showing an impl-lead/product ruling. AC-2.3 also requires loadCost.total to equal measured pull content, so the authoritative public contract cannot be established from current evidence.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/03-view-contents-report.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/03-view-contents-report/003-implementor.json\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/view-report.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/shared/inspect.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/inspect-view.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.3\",\"AC-2.4\",\"AC-2.5\",\"TD-Flow-2\",\"TD-Interface-ViewContentsReport\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-2.1 / TC-2.1: describe reads the stored thread_view/thread_view_band snapshot through thread-view internals, and inspect.view reports meta, band entries, gaps, storedTokens, config, and provenance from it; inspect-view.test.ts compares report and describe against raw stored rows.\",\"AC-2.2 / TC-2.2: inspect.view measures tail messages from threadView.pull; the boundary-advanced fixture asserts one abridged and one full tool result and verifies tail.tokens/loadCost.tailTokens equal measured served tail.\",\"AC-2.3 total parity behavior: compacted, boundary-advanced, and never-compacted tests assert loadCost.total equals an independent pull measured with the same estimator.\",\"AC-2.4 / TC-2.3: never-compacted test verifies meta null, bands [], gaps [], tail spans all pulled messages, bandTokens 0, and total parity.\",\"AC-2.5 purity/provenance for compacted views: sourceState is parsed from the stored row; read-only delta tests cover inspect.view and threadView.describe, including throwing-provider zero-provider legs.\",\"CLI/SDK DoD: sdk.ts exposes threadView.describe and inspect.view; cli/index.ts routes inspect view; inspect-view.test.ts asserts in-process CLI JSON parity for compacted and never-compacted threads.\",\"Production path audit